{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1538866-sabbat-antagonist-help","id":1538866,"title":"Sabbat Antagonist Help","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-07-18T14:17:26-07:00","id":1538866,"title":"Sabbat Antagonist Help","content":"I am storytelling in a Mage the Ascension game in a week and planned to use a 6th generation kindred as one of the antagonists. I am just having trouble nailing down which of the two sabbat pillars I want to use against them. Generally, the pillars are considered the Lasombra and the Tzimiscie. Does anyone have any suggestions about which of the two might be a better pick? I am planning for them to be fairly powerful in their particular magics with the Lasombra having abyss mysticism and the fiend having Koldunic sorcery (I know they generally don't have both flesh crafting and sorcery but there are practitioners of both in the lore)<br /> <br /> I generally just need insight on which would most likely give the players the most trouble in all of the relevant arenas of play socially, physically, mystically, politically, etc. I know it's an open-ended question but any thoughts or experiences to share would be very helpful.<br /> <br /> Also, I know mixed splat games are generally frowned on but its the kind of game my players were wanting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28506-carsusbloodking","name":"Carsusbloodking","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"16"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-18T16:27:56-07:00","id":1538878,"title":"","content":"I know almost nothing about Mage, so I can't say how vampires would challenge mage characters specifically.<br /> <br /> That being said, a 6th gen abyss mystic or koldun is likely not a Sabbat member, or just pretends to be one. There are exceptions, obviously.<br /> <br /> I would go for a Koldun, personally. Strong magic, easier to use (for characters as well as STs and players) than Abyss Mysticism to my understanding, combined with Auspex (reading minds and astral projection allow the NPG to be always one step ahead of the characters), Animalism (more ways to spy on the characters or mess with their minds) and Vicissitude (physical buffs for the vamp and his goons plus other custom effects to keep surprising the players) is great. Physical disciplines are always available and a 6th gen would have a good few dots in each at least. Domination is not in clan for Tzimisce, but a 6th gen would likely have at least the first 3 dots, sufficient to give commands and rewrite memories. 5 dots to possess bodies if you want to give the players more grief. Remember also that, for any discipline, a 6th gen has access to dots 6 and 7, which are custom powers, so feel free to come up with your own powers instead of feeling limited by the published material.<br /> Make sure he has good Fortitude so the mages don't just set him on fire at the first chance.<br /> <br /> Aside from disciplines (and attributes and skills), a 6th gen vamp probably has extensive backgrounds, minions, young and not so young vampires eager to please him to make an impression, powerful supernatural allies and ages of cunning and experience.<br /> <br /> A Lasombra has many of the same advantages, but I feel Koldun + Auspex, Animalism and Vicissitude is a more varied and effective tool kit than Abyss Mysticism + Dominate + Potence + Obtenebration.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16965-hermeticus","name":"Hermeticus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-18T17:22:39-07:00","id":1538880,"title":"","content":"The thing with Mage vs. Vampire is that the bloodsuckers just.....lose. Mages can create sunlight with relative ease, and with the right stats revert a vampire back into a mortal permanently regardless of Generation.<br /> <br /> So, you want to avoid head-to-head combat when using a vampire. Instead, you focus on the fact that they can get to anyone, use Dominate/Presence/Blood Bonding to turn anyone into a minion, and that their powers don't result in paradox. The interesting thing is that with the right discipline combo and Backgrounds, a 13th Generation played in this chess game style can be incredibly hard to deal with or defeat.<br /> <br /> Rather than getting into a punching match, the vampire will foreclose on the mages homes or their chantry. It's entirely possible for a vampire with Influence and Resources to just rezone the area where the Mages Node is, either to own it or disrupt the magic lines by changing the geomancy. Alternatively a vampire will have minions infiltrate the care facilities of the mages elder family members or replace teachers at the schools of their kids.<br /> <br /> In short a vampire fights by winning before a fight can happen.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-18T18:37:12-07:00","id":1538883,"title":"","content":"I wouldn't say the vampire just loses, because it depends a lot on what the Mages have and how prepared they are. And that isn't a bad thing, since the Mages are the PCs.<br /> <br /> But I would rather say the opposite: if they can't outsmart the vampire, this opponent is exceedingly dangerous.<br /> <br /> Mages are too dependent on how exactly they prepared themselves at any given moment. A 6th Gen Elder is likely to have a number of combat advantages, even without any combat focus on their build, that's just too much for a mortal to compete with.<br /> <br /> This should play like a chess game, and the vampire should begin with clear advantage. From there, it depends on the players being creative and smart to get out of sight and collect info on their enemy.<br /> <br /> One of the disadvantages of Mages is that they have rather small dice pools for their main schtick, and most of their better options require multiple successes. Nightfolk have a lot of oomph for their static powers, and can be hard to keep with.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-11T23:04:18-07:00","id":1541958,"title":"","content":"The most frightening villains are the ones who seem logical and convicted. The &quot;I wanna murder everybody slasher Jason/Myers/Krueger villains who are &quot;Evil, Because Evil&quot; villains are boring, and trite. You know, Vykos and all the other dumb Sabbat suspects.<br /> <br /> Have a villain whose motive are understandable, and logical, even though they're repulsive and odious (i.e., The weak don't deserve to live. If we don't kill them now, someone else worse will take advantage of them, and treat them much worse. We're doing them a favor.&quot;, etc.) And make the villain badass enough to give your coterie a good fight.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25666-illuminostro","name":"Illuminostro","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"166"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-13T10:44:54-07:00","id":1542067,"title":"","content":"I would like to think that most of us on these boards are fairly creative people and know a thing or two about pretty good characters that are relatable Illluminstro.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-13T13:22:25-07:00","id":1542071,"title":"","content":"Also, just because &quot;Cartoonish Evil Villains&quot; are unfashionable, doesn't mean they can't be fun. They just need to exist in their proper context. A splatterpunk game, where the villain is an unambiguous threat to be faced head-on, is very appropriate for this.<br /> <br /> (As an aside, I also want to stress that a perfectly logical villain is overrated, I think: the villain's motivations only need to make sense <i>to them</i>. Real Life shows that evil people are often rarely so logical or so &quot;correct&quot; as we'd like to think. Indeed, a lack of a sense of proportion is what makes some folk villainous in the first place.)<br /> <br /> For a Mage game like this, having a villain that's an indirect threat is more the proper speed. Plus, a 6th gen Elder vampire doesn't get to be that old or powerful by being imprudent. The Cabal should ideally not encounter their Cainite foe until they've worked through her web of conspiracies and underlings, and managed to corner her. Especially if she's AWARE the PCs are magic-users (whether she knows they have &quot;True Magick&quot; or not is immaterial).<br /> <br /> In some ways, the Influence, Resources, Contacts, Allies, and Retainers of the vampire are more likely to be an issue for most of the Chronicle. Even a sorcerous vampire, if they're smart, won't tip their hand about their arcane power right away. Not until they're sure what they're dealing with are <i>other magic-users</i>. Even then, they'll try to be circumspect about what capabilities they display.<br /> <br /> (On the other hand, there's something to be said about a sufficiently scary display of supernatural power. Scare the mortals into abandoning their efforts to disrupt the Cainite's plans. It won't work, because they're the PCs, but I could definitely see a vampire thinking that Kine can be cowed easily.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-13T16:27:06-07:00","id":1542078,"title":"","content":"As others pointed out, vampire antagonists versus mage PC's leads to painfully one-sided conflicts which ultimately aren't very fun. Been there, done that.<br /> <br /> The far better alternative is to provide the mage PC's a vampire frenemy, who's simply too valuable (and likely has too many fail-deadly plots) to just off, but too heinous in method for PC's to feel comfortable letting be. At the end of the day mages are still in proximity with a vampire, which is (and ought to be) something that makes mages' skins crawl, even without the possibility of mutual benefit or alliance.<br /> <br /> The crux of any vampire interaction for mages should be at what cost that interaction comes, and eventually how heavy that price is to pay. Be it in mages' morality, self respect, autonomy and agency, the very health of their Avatars (should one take a sip), or sleepers' lives around them. Exclusively antagonistic relationships exist at the nadir of that cost-benefit analysis, and as such make for poor thematic play.<br /> <br /> But on the other hand, untangling an individual elder's plots to the point they can be taken off the board safely can fuel an entire chronicle.<br /> <br /> Now, that said, when it comes to Tradition mages there's one clan that stands head and shoulders above the rest when it comes to deals with the devil and uncomfortable alliance...and it ain't the Tremere. It's <i>because of</i> the Tremere, as that clan is the Tzimisce. They're occult scholars, transcendentalists (in their own way), eminently polite and skillful with etiquette and protocol, and more than anything else, value expanding their horizons (in their own way).<br /> <br /> And best of all that's canon, as while Hermetics and Tremere have a...rocky...relationship, Hermetics and Tzimisce tend to get along <i>fantastically</i>. Nobody hates their enemies quite each other, and they definitely have one big enemy in common.<br /> <br /> So the best way to kick that off is with an elder Tzimisce who knows a thing or two about mages (quite a few do), and has...a proposal. That Tzimisce knows a bit about what local Technocrats are up to, maybe even has a Technocrat informant or blood-slave by way of the alphabet agency of your choice. That Tzimisce also has a chantry full of Tremere they'd very much like to see ushered off this (im)mortal coil.<br /> <br /> And if that chantry so happens to...you know, go boom...if a cabal of mages were somehow responsible, that cabal just might find themselves the recipient of a sudden and inexplicable windfall of valuable information about the Technocracy. So long as all that other heinous shit Tzimisce elders get up to goes conveniently overlooked for a time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude0e","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","name":"Theodrim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-13T16:39:06-07:00","id":1542080,"title":"","content":"Sorry for double-posting, but concerned about spam filter. Going off that...<br /> <br /> Oh, and the Tzimisce might know about a secret Nephandus or two...but this time, the cabal needs to make the city's Sheriff or even a Prince disappear. It's only fair, you now. Never find the swath of missing vagrants. It's probably for the better other Tradition mages or even the Council never found out about this, they don't take kindly to mages working with vampires so openly. It'd be a shame if someone tipped them off. It wouldn't be the friendly neighborhood Tzimisce, of course...they're a <i>friend</i>, they'd never do something so impolite.<br /> <br /> Well, at least now that mutual trust and respect's founded, time to get onto the real work, right? All these strange goings-on has attracted an Archon, or maybe the Technocrats are sniffing around all these mysterious vampire-related explosions that certainly aren't being done by magic (and if they found out somehow, it definitely wouldn't have been through that Technocrat retainer). Maybe more mutual back-scratching is in order? The Tzimisce arranges for the cabal's enemies to disappear, if the cabal just makes another of the Tzimisce's enemies (or two) disappear. How convenient!<br /> <br /> No, the city's Nosferatu haven't disappeared and that's definitely not the foundations for a cathedral of flesh being laid in the city's sewers. Weird how that got there, the Tzimisce will definitely look into it. It's probably the Baali up to whatever it is they do at night. Hey, Life mage! here's a neat trick...wanna learn it and add it to your repertoire? all you gotta do is just run this package to the next city over, never mind it's leaking blood and probably whimpering for the sweet release of death. It's for the best, trust me...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude0e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","name":"Theodrim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-16T01:44:20-07:00","id":1542238,"title":"","content":"Personally I like the idea of a Tzimisce fleshcrafter for the body-horror aspect. Having bizarre fleshcrafted creations turning up left and right would keep your protags on their toes, even if the actual horrors aren't that deadly. <br /> <br /> One problem I've found with smart Mage players is that tey will try everything to short cut the process of discovering who the villain is so you need to be well armed with a lot of diversionary information that they can discover and very strict with how they use divinatory effects of any kind.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11490-dogstar","name":"Dogstar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11490_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}